-- R-X2, upstream smucclaw/l4-ide#956: a WITH supply is checked against the type
-- the BINDER was declared with, not against whatever the caller's own scope
-- binds that spelling to.
--
-- `bad` has a WHERE local also called `rate`, and a local shadows a section
-- GIVEN absolutely. So the expression on the right of IS is a piece of text.
-- The name on the LEFT of IS is not the local, though: it is the input of the
-- rule being called, which the heading declares as a number, and that is what
-- the value has to fit.
--
-- Before this was checked the file passed `l4 check` clean and died in `l4 run`
-- as "Internal error ... running bin op with invalid operation / value
-- combination": a type error escaping the type checker as a bug report.
-- Confirmed 2026-09-08 against two independently built binaries at 6e9b57bb.
--
-- The remedy is to supply a number. See doc/reference/syntax/section-given.md.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 0.05

GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS 100 TIMES rate

GIVETH A NUMBER
bad MEANS scaled WITH rate IS rate
    WHERE
        rate MEANS "5 percent"
